### references/installation-registration.md  [docs]
- On first use, the bundled client makes a best-effort non-billable
- `beatra.installations.register` call for this package. Registration records the
- package slug, version, platform, and stable external installation reference; it
- does not replace Device Authorization and never asks for narrower package
- scopes.
- The non-secret `~/.beatra/registrations.json` cache suppresses another
- registration until the package version or agent environment changes or
- 24 hours pass. Registration failure must never block the user's requested
- creative task. An unknown but well-formed package slug is accepted and
- recorded as unrecognized so package release never depends on a synchronized
- backend registry deployment.
+ On first use, and again when the version, agent environment, channel, network
+ route, install source or installation reference changes or 24 hours pass, the
+ bundled client makes one best-effort, non-billable
+ `beatra.installations.register` call for this package. It is the only reporting call
+ the Skill makes, it does not replace Device Authorization, it never asks for
+ narrower package scopes, and its failure never blocks the user's requested
+ task. It records:
+ - the package, its version, the agent environment (`platform`), and the
+   stable installation reference;
+ - the distribution channel and locale fixed when the package was built;
+ - the network route this computer uses and why (see the MCP connection
+   reference);
+ - where this copy was installed from, when known: a source file Beatra adds to
+   copies it hands to a store or its website, a store client's own record in
+   the Skill directory, or the agent's `install-source --guess`;
+ - coarse runtime facts: operating system and version, processor architecture,
+   Python version, interface language, and time-zone offset.
+ It never sends user names, file paths, environment variables, prompts, or tool
+ details. Beatra uses these fields to understand which stores and networks
+ people install from, as its privacy policy describes, and clears the runtime
+ facts when the account is deleted.
+ A per-installation cache in `~/.beatra/updates/` suppresses another
+ registration until the version, agent environment, channel, network route, install
+ source or installation reference changes, or 24 hours pass. An unknown but well-formed package
+ slug is accepted and recorded as unrecognized, so package release never
+ depends on a synchronized backend registry deployment.

### references/mcp-connection.md  [docs]
+ ```text
+ ```
+ The host follows this computer's network route, described below.
+ ## Network route
+ Beatra serves two networks: the international hosts, and the mainland China
+ hosts `mcp.beatra.cn`, `api.beatra.cn`, `www.beatra.cn`, `cdn.beatra.cn` and
+ `console.beatra.cn`. The saved credential works on both. Packages of the
+ mainland China (`cn`) channel always use the mainland hosts and cannot change
+ network (`network` shows `"policy":"cn"`). Other packages choose once a day,
+ before their first command: the client asks Beatra which network suits this computer,
+ in a small request that carries no credential and no installation identity,
+ and records the answer in `~/.beatra/network.json`. Approval pages, console and
+ top-up links, uploads, and result downloads then follow the chosen network.
+ python3 scripts/mcp_client.py network
+ python3 scripts/mcp_client.py network --use auto
+ `network` shows the current choice. Only when the user asks for a specific
+ network, run `network --use cn` (mainland China) or `network --use ai`
+ (international): it first checks that Beatra answers on that network and
+ refuses otherwise; packages of the `cn` channel refuse `--use`. If commands start failing to connect after a network was
+ chosen this way, run `network --use auto`. A request that failed is never
+ resent on the other network; the next command decides again unless a network was chosen with
+ `network --use`.
+ On the mainland China network the approval page offers WeChat, phone and email
+ sign-in. If the user cannot find their sign-in method, or wants to sign in with
+ Google, run `python3 scripts/authorize.py --approval-link ai`: it shows the same
+ approval on Beatra's international site, and the network does not change;
+ `--approval-link auto` goes back. When you give the user a console or top-up
+ link on the mainland network, remind them to sign in the way they did before
+ (phone, email, or the same WeChat): scanning with a different WeChat creates a
+ separate account. If credits do not appear after a top-up, first check that
+ they signed in to the same account.

